<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Sui Dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">581 CE – 618 CE · capital Daxing (Chang'an)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The short dynasty that reunited China in 589, built the Grand Canal and laid the institutional foundations of the Tang.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wen-of-sui">Yang Jian</a>, an aristocrat of mixed Han and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/xianbei">Xianbei</a> background and father-in-law of a <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/northern-zhou">Northern Zhou</a> emperor, seized power as regent and took the throne in 581 as Emperor Wen. He built a new capital, Daxing, beside old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a>, absorbed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/western-liang-555-587">Western Liang</a> in 587 and conquered the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chen-dynasty">Chen dynasty</a> in 589.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wen-of-sui">Emperor Wen</a> issued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaihuang-code">Kaihuang Code</a>, kept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/equal-field-system">equal-field</a> land system and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fubing-system">fubing</a> militia, reformed local administration, took regular <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/census">censuses</a> and began recruiting officials by examination. He was a fervent patron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-yang-of-sui">Emperor Yang</a> built the eastern capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> and linked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-canal">Grand Canal</a>, using vast forced labour.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Three failed invasions of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/goguryeo">Goguryeo</a> between 612 and 614 drained manpower and sparked revolts across the empire. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-yang-of-sui">Emperor Yang</a> withdrew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangzhou">Jiangdu</a>, where he was murdered in 618; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozu-of-tang">Li Yuan</a>, who had taken <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a>, founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a>, which kept most Sui institutions.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sui-dynasty.jpg" alt="Sui Dynasty" width="320" height="309"><figcaption>Image: Ian Kiu · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cheui_Dynasty_581_CE.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>581 CE – 618 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Daxing (Chang'an)</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Yang Jian (Emperor Wen), Yang Guang (Emperor Yang), Yang You (Emperor Gong)</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Mahayana Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Middle Chinese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sui</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=600&amp;focus=sui-dynasty" aria-label="Sui Dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7449 935 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sui Dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7769 1191L7771 1192M7769 1191L7769 1191M7769 1191L7920 1337M7769 1191L8057 1267M7769 1191L7855 1179M7769 1191L7616 1132M7769 1191L7559 1070"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7771 1192h0M7769 1191h0M7920 1337h0M8057 1267h0M7855 1179h0M7616 1132h0M7559 1070h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7769 1191h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7769 1191h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=600&amp;focus=sui-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
